---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Sect from '../components/Sect.astro';
---

<Base
  title="About"
  manName="ABOUT"
  description="About ALO (Gene): software team lead at 365 Retail Markets, volunteer tech lead for the Win Metta nonprofit, and weekend teacher."
>
  <Sect name="Name">
    <h1>
      about: <span title="Aung Lwin Oo">ALO</span>, known to some as Gene
    </h1>
    <p class="lede">
      ninegene is my username. I build software, improve how teams develop and
      operate it, and teach what I learn.
    </p>
  </Sect>

  <Sect name="Work">
    <p>
      I've been at{' '}
      <a href="https://365retailmarkets.com/">365 Retail Markets</a>
      for more than ten years, now as a software team lead. The company makes
      self-checkout kiosks and point-of-sale systems for unattended retail; I've
      worked on the <a href="https://365retailmarkets.com/adm">back office</a>
      and the{' '}
      <a href="https://365retailmarkets.com/mm6-markets">kiosk and POS</a>
      side, from frontend to backend to infrastructure, as part of the team that
      builds them.
    </p>
    <p>The kinds of things I do there:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Build and maintain backend services and the point-of-sale software that
        talks to them, in Java, Kotlin, TypeScript, JavaScript and Python.</li>
      <li>Run cloud infrastructure on AWS, managed as code with Terraform (and
        earlier with CloudFormation and the AWS CDK).</li>
      <li>Automate releases: years before AI coding tools, I built a chat bot that
        let the team build, deploy and release from Slack.</li>
      <li>Use AI to make development and support faster: MCP servers that connect
        AI agents to databases, the data warehouse, logs, traces and metrics so
        support, QA and developers can troubleshoot with evidence; agent skills
        and repeatable cloud development environments; and documentation
        generated from reading code across many repositories.</li>
    </ul>
  </Sect>

  <Sect name="Volunteering">
    <p>
      I helped found <a href="https://winmetta.org/">Win Metta</a>, a California
      nonprofit that offers Buddhist meditation and education programs in
      Burmese and English, and serve as its secretary and tech lead. I build and
      run its
      <a href="/projects/winmetta-platform/">web platform</a> and the tools its
      volunteers use.
    </p>
  </Sect>

  <Sect name="Teaching">
    <p>
      Learning and teaching are what I enjoy most about this work. On weekends I
      teach a small group of middle and high school students, for free. The
      <a href="/learn/">learn</a> page lists the free resources I'm building.
    </p>
  </Sect>

  <Sect name="Tools">
    <p>
      Vim, VS Code and IntelliJ IDEA for code; Obsidian for notes; mise for tool
      versions; Claude, ChatGPT and Gemini as AI assistants. More on the
      <a href="/uses/">uses</a> page.
    </p>
  </Sect>

  <Sect name="Contact">
    <p>
      Say hello or ask a question in the issues of
      <a href="https://github.com/ninegene/ninegene/issues">github.com/ninegene/ninegene</a>. I'm not on LinkedIn or X.
    </p>
  </Sect>
</Base>
